 How to Check If a Kafka Producer or Consumer is Down
1. Kafka Producer
Kafka producers don’t maintain a persistent connection like consumers;
they just send messages. However, you can detect problems by:

a. Producer Client Metrics & Logs
Kafka producer exposes metrics via JMX or your monitoring system:
record-send-rate: Messages sent per second
record-error-rate: Error rate when sending messages
request-latency-avg: Average request latency
If you see high error rate or no records sent over time,
the producer might be down or stuck.
Check application logs for exceptions like:
TimeoutException
NetworkException
NotEnoughReplicasException

Application Health Checks
Implement health endpoints (e.g., Spring Boot Actuator /health) that:
Attempt a lightweight send or check the producer state.
Use circuit breakers or retry frameworks to surface persistent failures.

Consumers maintain a connection with Kafka brokers as part of a consumer group.
Here are ways to check if a consumer is down:
kafka-consumer-groups.sh --bootstrap-server <broker> --describe --group <group-name>
This shows:

Consumers in the group
Partition assignments
Lag (messages behind the latest offset)
If no active consumers appear for the group or lag does not decrease,
consumers might be down or stuck.
Kafka broker logs detect when consumers leave groups due to missed heartbeats.

Metrics to monitor:
consumer-fetch-manager-metrics.records-consumed-rate
consumer-fetch-manager-metrics.fetch-latency-avg
consumer-coordinator-metrics.commit-latency-avg
If these drop or stop reporting, consumer might be down.

c.Monitoring Consumer Heartbeats
Kafka consumers send heartbeats to the group coordinator.
Missed heartbeats trigger rebalances.
You can monitor heartbeat rates via JMX or metrics exporter tools.

| Component    | How to Check                                                     | Tools/Commands                        |
| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| **Producer** | Monitor metrics/logs, error rates, health endpoints              | JMX, Spring Boot Actuator, Logs       |
| **Consumer** | Monitor group membership and lag, heartbeat metrics, broker logs | `kafka-consumer-groups.sh`, JMX, Logs |
